      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The phase-root representation specializes at φ=0 to Gram-point sampling, where the Hardy-Z normalization turns negative real intersections into failures of the normalized Gram sign rule; reindexing the directional moments by Gram number then constrains the aggregate size of the same sampled sequence through second- and fourth-moment growth without restoring pointwise sign alternation.",
